 @yapweehow  'Temperature' is mostly dependent on the cooling solution used. In terms of actual 'heat output', the 6800XT's power consumption is not all that bad, relatively speaking, so heat output matches accordingly.

If you don't understand the difference between temperature and heat output, here's an example to get you thinking:
A passively cooled GT1030 may reach upwards of 80-90c under load, while a GTX2070 with a nice AIB cooler might reach only 60-70c under load. The GT1030 does not produce more heat than the GTX2070 though.

